From: Uke platform maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: keep WCN6750 out of IMPS so idle links wake fast

An SSH session to the tablet stalls for a moment on the first keystroke
after the link has been idle, while a local console does not.  The link is
otherwise healthy: 270 Mbit/s receive, -51 dBm, and a continuous ping keeps
the stall away entirely.

Two power-save mechanisms are involved and only one is reachable from
userspace.  IEEE80211's STA power-save mode is what `iw dev wlan0 set
power_save off` clears, through `arvif->ps` and `WMI_STA_PS_MODE_DISABLED`.
IMPS is a separate pdev parameter: `ath11k_mac_op_start()` asks the firmware
for `WMI_PDEV_PARAM_IDLE_PS_CONFIG` whenever `hw_params.idle_ps` is set, and
nothing in debugfs or the module parameters can turn it off afterwards.

With STA power-save already off the stall persisted, and a ping every 30
seconds still kept it away, so the remaining suspect is IMPS itself: the
whole wireless subsystem sleeps when idle and its exit is slow enough to be
felt on the first packet.  Disabling it costs some idle power on a tablet
that keeps Wi-Fi associated anyway.

Only the wcn6750 hw_params entry changes; every other ath11k board keeps
whatever its own table asks for.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -617,7 +617,14 @@
 					BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP),
 		.supports_monitor = false,
 		.supports_shadow_regs = true,
-		.idle_ps = true,
+		/*
+		 * IMPS lets the whole wireless subsystem sleep when idle.  On this
+		 * tablet its exit costs enough that an idle SSH session stalls for
+		 * a moment on the first keystroke, and `iw set power_save off`
+		 * cannot turn it off: the STA power-save mode and this pdev
+		 * parameter are separate.  Uke keeps IMPS disabled.
+		 */
+		.idle_ps = false,
 		.supports_sta_ps = true,
 		.coldboot_cal_mm = true,
 		.coldboot_cal_ftm = true,
